\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Lemma}
\title{Kept forms compose}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{Let the edge weights be strictly positive and the graph
connected. Let #{K} and #{K'} be nonempty sets of vertices
with #{K} contained in #{K'}. For every function #{u} on
#{K}, the \vocabk{kept form}{fdip-00DF} of #{u} equals the
minimum, over functions on #{K'} that extend #{u}, of the
kept form on #{K'}.}

\proof{
\p{Let #{h} be the counting inner product of \ref{fdip-00DF},
and write the energy as #{h(x,(-L_w)x)}. \ref{fdip-00DH}
supplies a kept form on #{K'} and a unique energy-minimizing
extension of any prescribed values there. The identity
includes #{K=K'} and #{K'=V}. When #{K'=V}, the kept form on
#{K'} is the energy. When #{K=K'}, the only extension of
#{u} from #{K} to #{K'} is #{u} itself. Take a function
#{u} on #{K}. Every extension of #{u} to the
whole vertex set restricts to an extension of #{u} to #{K'},
and the inner minimum depends only on that restriction.
Minimizing over the restriction therefore equals minimizing
over all extensions. The common value is the kept form of
#{u}. Attainment and uniqueness of the full extension are
those of \ref{fdip-00DH}.}

\p{Suppose #{K} is a proper subset of #{K'}. Let #{U} be the
vertices of #{K'} outside #{K}, and let #{\iota_U} be the
inclusion of functions on #{K'} supported on #{U}. Let #{S'}
be the self-adjoint operator of the kept form on #{K'} for
the counting product on #{K'}. The form on functions vanishing
on #{K} is the compression #{\iota_U^{\dagger} S' \iota_U}. When #{K'=V},
#{S'} is #{-L_w} and that compression is #{\iota_U^{\dagger}(-L_w)\iota_U}.
If a function on #{K'} vanishes on #{K}
and has kept energy #{0}, its minimizing extension has energy
#{0}, hence is constant, hence is #{0}. The compression is
therefore positive definite. That positivity is not a claim
that the kept form on #{K'} is positive definite. The square
completion of \ref{fdip-00DH}, applied to this compression,
attains the minimum over extensions from #{K} to #{K'}.}
}
